---
// A link's arrow: → a page of this site, ↗ one that leaves it, ← the way back. Screen readers skip it.
// The gap to its word is the arrow's own padding, after the word, or before it for ←, so callers
// write no space: an inline-block takes no part in its link's underline, which then stops at the word.
const glyph = await Astro.slots.render('default');
---

<span
  aria-hidden="true"
  class:list={['inline-block font-sans', glyph.trim() === '←' ? 'pe-1' : 'ps-1']}
  set:html={glyph}
/>
